{# IN·07 — six months of filings, the line the map cannot draw.

   The one reading on this surface whose window is not the page's month: the map,
   the register and every other chart read the one month, but a trend needs more
   than a month to be a line, so the repository carries its own six
   ({@see IncidentRepository::monthlyFiledCounts}). One filter still drives it —
   the category chips, the lens and the search narrow the line the same way they
   narrow the register.

   The drawing is the chart layer's ({@see _charts.html.twig}); this partial
   fetches the months and hands them over as a labelled series. #}
{% import '@UhifadhiIncident/dashboard/_charts.html.twig' as charts %}
{% set months = dashboard.monthlyCounts %}
<div class="c chartcard" data-w="trend">
    <span class="tab">Incidents over time<span class="src">· filed per month{% if months is not empty %} · {{ (months|keys|first ~ '-01')|date('M')|lower }}–{{ (months|keys|last ~ '-01')|date('M')|lower }} {{ (months|keys|last ~ '-01')|date('Y') }}{% endif %}</span></span>
    {% set series = [] %}
    {% for key, count in months %}
        {% set series = series|merge([{
            label: (key ~ '-01')|date('M')|lower,
            value: count,
            title: (key ~ '-01')|date('F') ~ ': ' ~ count,
        }]) %}
    {% endfor %}
    {% if series is not empty %}{{ charts.line(series) }}{% endif %}
</div>
